{
  "topics": [
    {
      "id": "hlv.t01",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The linear playout controller's primary controller host is flint-play.hlv.invalid. Operators use it to inspect the active channel schedule before handing off a rundown.",
        "f2": "On 2026-02-12, the linear playout controller's primary controller host changed to willow-play.hlv.invalid after the previous host began dropping heartbeat reports.",
        "d": "The linear playout controller records each rundown handoff in the operations journal so the next shift can distinguish planned transitions from retries."
      },
      "query": "What is the linear playout controller's current primary controller host?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t02",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The transcode delivery worker writes completed outputs to hlv-xcode-fen-renditions. Its completion record is emitted only after the object is readable.",
        "f2": "On 2026-03-04, the transcode delivery worker's output bucket changed to hlv-xcode-dune-renditions to separate new deliveries from a backlog in the previous bucket.",
        "d": "The transcode delivery worker retries object publication separately from encoding, so a storage timeout does not trigger another full transcode."
      },
      "query": "Which output bucket does the transcode delivery worker currently use?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t03",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The subtitle alignment pipeline takes pending jobs from hlv-subalign-morrow-q. Workers acknowledge a job after the aligned track has passed format validation.",
        "f2": "On 2026-03-11, the subtitle alignment pipeline's pending jobs queue changed to hlv-subalign-kestrel-q because the previous queue's retry backlog was delaying fresh work.",
        "d": "The subtitle alignment pipeline keeps failed alignment attempts visible to the captioning desk, along with the source asset and language code."
      },
      "query": "What is the subtitle alignment pipeline's current pending jobs queue?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t04",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The DRM key rotation process runs on a cadence of 31 min (hlv-keyrot). Each run logs the affected key set before the licence servers reload it.",
        "f2": "On 2026-04-08, the DRM key rotation process changed to a cadence of 59 min (hlv-keyrot) to give the licence-server replicas more time to converge between runs.",
        "d": "The DRM key rotation process raises an alert if a licence-server replica has not acknowledged the newly published key set."
      },
      "query": "What is the DRM key rotation process's current rotation cadence?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t05",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "Dynamic ad insertion uses hlv-splice-bloom as its default splice policy. The ad decision record retains the policy selected for each break.",
        "f2": "On 2026-04-16, the default splice policy for dynamic ad insertion changed to hlv-splice-drift after break-boundary checks showed fewer short fills with the new policy.",
        "d": "Dynamic ad insertion records break-boundary decisions alongside the ad decision record, making short fills traceable without replaying the stream."
      },
      "query": "What is the current default splice policy for dynamic ad insertion?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t06",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The asset catalogue index uses hlv-mam-schema-6.1 as its metadata schema version. Index readers reject documents missing a required asset identifier.",
        "f2": "On 2026-05-06, the asset catalogue index's metadata schema version changed to hlv-mam-schema-7.3 to support the new rights-window fields.",
        "d": "The asset catalogue index is rebuilt from media asset manager records; the search copy is not the source of truth for rights metadata."
      },
      "query": "What metadata schema version does the asset catalogue index currently use?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t07",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The overnight rundown reconciler's scheduled run time is hlv-rundown-vaskira/02:51Z. It compares the automation log with the approved rundown after the late feed closes.",
        "f2": "On 2026-05-19, the overnight rundown reconciler's scheduled run time changed to hlv-rundown-meltrix/03:16Z so the late feed could finish before reconciliation starts.",
        "d": "The overnight rundown reconciler reports unmatched events to playout operations and leaves the approved rundown unchanged."
      },
      "query": "What is the overnight rundown reconciler's current scheduled run time?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t08",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The mezzanine ingest gateway's active ingest host is hazel-ingest.hlv.invalid. New arrivals receive a checksum before they enter the media asset manager.",
        "f2": "On 2026-06-02, the mezzanine ingest gateway's active ingest host changed to basalt-ingest.hlv.invalid while the previous host's storage controller was serviced.",
        "d": "The mezzanine ingest gateway quarantines arrivals whose supplied manifest does not match the uploaded media."
      },
      "query": "Which host is active for the mezzanine ingest gateway?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t09",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The caption distribution bridge delivers approved tracks through hlv-captions-delta. Delivery receipts are attached to the corresponding programme record.",
        "f2": "On 2026-06-17, the caption distribution bridge's delivery channel changed to hlv-captions-aperture after the downstream receiver moved to a new subscription.",
        "d": "The caption distribution bridge sends only tracks that have cleared subtitle QC and retains a receipt for each downstream handoff."
      },
      "query": "What is the caption distribution bridge's current delivery channel?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t10",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The licence request router prefers hlv-region-nq1 as its serving region. It falls back only when the regional health probe fails.",
        "f2": "On 2026-07-01, the licence request router's preferred serving region changed to hlv-region-yp5 after capacity was added nearer the evening audience peak.",
        "d": "The licence request router logs the region chosen for each request without recording the viewer's playback token."
      },
      "query": "What is the licence request router's current preferred serving region?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t11",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The ad beacon archive's event retention period is hlv-beacon-tamarind/21d. Archive records are used to investigate discrepancies between insertion and billing counts.",
        "d": "The ad beacon archive groups events by programme and break identifier; investigators can compare those groups with insertion logs."
      },
      "query": "What is the ad beacon archive's event retention period?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t12",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "Media asset intake uses hlv-intake-Crestscan as its ingest validator tool. Validation results stay with the intake record when an asset is accepted.",
        "d": "Media asset intake holds a submission for review when its manifest and media disagree, rather than silently changing the supplied metadata."
      },
      "query": "Which ingest validator tool does media asset intake use?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t13",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The transcode duty desk uses hlv-dash-Firebreak as its health dashboard. The on-call engineer checks worker saturation there during delivery delays.",
        "d": "The transcode duty desk hands unresolved delivery delays to the next shift with the affected asset IDs and the last observed worker state."
      },
      "query": "What is the transcode duty desk's health dashboard?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t14",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The live encoder preset's default output profile is hlv-encode-curlew-1080p. The profile is applied when a channel has no programme-specific override.",
        "f2": "On 2026-07-09, the live encoder preset's default output profile changed to hlv-encode-heron-1080p for a trial of steadier motion handling on live sport.",
        "d": "Programme-specific encoder overrides are recorded with the transmission booking, so operators can distinguish them from the default.",
        "f3": "The live encoder preset's default output profile is back to hlv-encode-curlew-1080p after the trial showed unacceptable detail loss in studio graphics."
      },
      "query": "What is the live encoder preset's current default output profile?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t15",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The subtitle QC gate allows a maximum timing drift of 148 ms (hlv-subqc). Tracks beyond the limit are held for review before distribution.",
        "f2": "On 2026-07-14, the subtitle QC gate's maximum timing drift changed to 103 ms (hlv-subqc) to evaluate a tighter acceptance threshold.",
        "d": "The subtitle QC gate reports the worst measured offset with the affected track, giving reviewers a starting point for correction.",
        "f3": "The subtitle QC gate's maximum timing drift is back to 148 ms (hlv-subqc) because the tighter threshold held otherwise acceptable archive captions."
      },
      "query": "What maximum timing drift does the subtitle QC gate currently allow?"
    },
    {
      "id": "hlv.t16",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The DRM failover broker's backup licence vendor is hlv-vendor-Briargate. The broker uses the backup only when its primary route is unhealthy.",
        "f2": "On 2026-08-03, the DRM failover broker's backup licence vendor changed to hlv-vendor-Estralin for a regional failover trial.",
        "d": "The DRM failover broker records each route switch and alerts the licence operations desk when backup serving begins.",
        "f3": "The DRM failover broker's backup licence vendor is back to hlv-vendor-Briargate after the trial exposed inconsistent acknowledgement of key updates."
      },
      "query": "Who is the DRM failover broker's current backup licence vendor?"
    }
  ],
